nt-dependent selection helpers during construction.\n- Preserve shared history recording/pruning for edits and indentation, exact live-edit identity tracking, undo/redo restoration, inherited-edit maintenance, and no-op redo preservation. Keep idle pruning active.\n- In `tests/sql/explorer/cursor_history.py`, construct the eviction-test history with all required arguments: `max_checkpoints=2`, `checkpoint_timer=60.0`, and `checkpoint_max_characters=1000`. Retain explicit transaction checkpoints and every eviction, metadata-bound, text, selection, and preferred-column assertion.\n- Extend its parameterized reset regression for both `load_text()` and the `text` setter. Create mounted cursors and reversed selections across several rows with distinct preferred columns, populate undo and redo, then replace with shorter single-line text and empty text.\n- In `tests/agent_tools/completion_readiness.py`, complete the idle fixture with empty undo/redo stacks, cursor-history metadata, and a callback invoking the real pruning method. Retain assertions that idle reopens retained suggestions and leaves dismissed suggestions closed.\n- Fully read edited files through their final continuation before writing. Preserve recovered tests/documentation, changelog history, and authenticated task history. Record the correction through the managed changelog mechanism without changing package or README versions.\n- Public APIs, runtime dependencies, Python 3.8–3.14/Textual support, protected workflows, and diagnostic interfaces remain unchanged.\n\n## Required behavior retained\n\n- Anchored Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down selection preserves independent preferred columns through reversal, short lines, and boundaries without creating cursors.\n- Independent multicursor movement/editing supports multiple cursors per row, selection merging, atomic undo/redo, and exact-position Shift+Up/Down toggling.\n- Ctrl+C, `cp`, and Ctrl+X retain document-order fragments, including empties. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Keyboard, command, and terminal paste use matching fragments, then matching lines ignoring one trailing line ending, then whole-text repetition. Preserve metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Keep SQL readable with thin primary/secondary carets, vertical bars where supported and occupied-cell underline fallback.\n- Preserve the selected narrow UI repairs, supersampling, comparison evidence, and strict diagnostics. The inspected published-head picker PNG supplies no reason for another rendering change.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\nPrivate workers execute no programs, tests, installs, or rendering.\n\n- Run the two failing modules first on canonical Python 3.11, Python 3.8 minimum dependencies, and Python 3.13/3.14 latest dependencies.\n- Reset regressions must assert one valid primary cursor, no secondary cursors or obsolete preferences, cleared history/snapshots, safe rendering after layout settles, and typing at only the reset cursor. Undo/redo must not resurrect the old document or cursors. Retain construction and unmounted-reset coverage.\n- Run existing history lifecycle, multicursor, clipboard, selection/movement, caret, menu-viewport, checkbox/selector, SVG-evidence, supersampling, and capture-lifecycle regressions.\n- Require fresh exact-head static/lint/format/type, artifact, compatibility/minimum-dependency, SDK, and aggregate checks. Obtain canonical coverage JSON; retain **98.03% branch**, **98.92% combined**, **99.22% statement**, subsystem floors, and debt baselines. The failed coverage test run establishes no new ratchet shortfall.\n- Capture the corrected isolated candidate on GitHub and independently inspect all 46 full PNGs and geometry results before correction publication. Bind evidence to the actual source, candidate, checkpoint, base, task, plan, and dependencies; published-head captures do not validate new edits.\n\n## Review and completion\n\n- Obtain fresh independent plan review before coding and complete implementation review afterward, including every diff continuation and the RPi companion implementation. Earlier incomplete reviews supply no approval.\n- Revalidate changed heads and dev bases. Preserve provenance, credentials, genuine-input holds, owner vetoes, and applicable real-owner exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator must verify completion and safe activation of recommendation-policy companion work and recovery of agents waiting solely on routine choices, retaining question/resolver records and security holds.\n- Monitor PR #9 and every task-related companion or repair PR through successful dev merges and required post-merge validation. This bounded correction does not replace that overall completion requirement.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"a07d171e6d4a09c77a547e9facb213584f0e78ae82abcdb5c2ab3d0a7c6c4974","text":"# Correct PR #9’s unmounted-reset test context\n\n## Summary\n\nContinue from head `a30ce3df206677c416b34e06b99e97e80764d1f1` against pinned dev `8955054742d6df6c4700c6e9db815ff3cb9efc3b`.\n\nComplete current-head feedback identifies four failures in the unmounted-reset regression. Python 3.8/3.9 lack an event loop; Python 3.10–3.12 lack an active Textual app. The independent resolver selected **Active app context**. No material question remains.\n\n## Implementation and compatibility\n\n- In `tests/sql/explorer/cursor_history.py`, wrap the existing parameterized unmounted-reset test body in an asynchronous exercise invoked through `asyncio.run()`. Construct `SqlExplorerApp(FakeSession())` and enter `app.run_test()` before constructing either detached editor.\n- Keep both editors outside the mounted widget tree. Explicitly assert that each remains unmounted after construction and relevant operations.\n- Preserve all four parameter combinations, construction checks, no-op undo/redo checks, reset assertions, cursor/preferences cleanup, and empty history/snapshot assertions.\n- Retain the mounted reset/render/type regressions and shared history lifecycle unchanged. Do not catch or suppress Textual lifecycle errors, skip environments, or weaken assertions.\n- Preserve the complete checkpoint, recovered source/documentation, changelog history, and authenticated task history. Fully read edited files before writing; record the correction through the managed changelog mechanism without changing package versions.\n- Public APIs, production behavior, dependencies, diagnostic interfaces, and Python 3.8–3.14/Textual compatibility remain unchanged.\n\n## Feature requirements retained\n\n- Preserve anchored Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down selection, independent preferred columns, multiple cursors per row, selection merging, atomic editing/history, and exact-position Shift+Up/Down toggling.\n- Preserve document-order Ctrl+C/`cp`/Ctrl+X fragments, including empties; entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing. One unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Preserve shared keyboard/command/terminal paste: matching fragments first, matching lines ignoring one trailing line ending second, otherwise whole-text repetition. Retain metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Preserve readable SQL with thin primary/secondary carets, supported vertical bars and occupied-cell underline fallback.\n- Retain selected narrow UI repairs, supersampled captures, comparison evidence, and strict diagnostics. Inspected published-head PNGs supply no reason for another rendering change.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\nPrivate workers execute no programs, tests, installs, or rendering.\n\n- First run all four corrected cases and the complete cursor-history module on GitHub: Python 3.8 minimum/latest, canonical Python 3.11, and Python 3.13/3.14 latest. Require explicit unmounted-state assertions to pass.\n- Run adjacent lifecycle and completion-readiness tests, then focused multicursor, clipboard, movement/selection, caret, menu-viewport, checkbox/selector, SVG-evidence, supersampling, and capture-lifecycle coverage.\n- Require exact-head lint/format/type, artifact, Python compatibility/minimum-dependency, SDK conformance, and aggregate fast checks.\n- Obtain fresh canonical coverage JSON. Preserve **98.03% branch**, **98.92% combined**, **99.22% statement**, subsystem floors, and debt baselines. The failed test run establishes no new coverage shortfall.\n- Capture the corrected isolated candidate through the trusted GitHub route. Independently inspect all 46 full PNGs and geometry results before correction publication, retaining picker comparisons. Bind evidence to actual source, candidate, checkpoint, dev base, task, plan, and dependencies.\n\n## Review and completion\n\n- Obtain independent plan review before coding and complete independent implementation review afterward. Review every diff continuation, including previously unfinished diagnostic/capture modules, associated tests, and immutable companion implementation and exact-commit CI evidence. Earlier partial review supplies no approval.\n- Revalidate whenever the head or dev base changes. Preserve complete provenance, credentials, genuine-input holds, owner vetoes, and applicable real-owner exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator must verify completion and safe activation of the RPi recommendation-policy work and restart agents waiting solely on routine implementation choices, preserving question/resolver records and security holds.\n- Monitor PR #9, the RPi policy/restart companion work, and every task-related repair PR until all merge successfully into `dev` and required post-merge validation completes. This test correction alone does not complete that objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"ba4a97a05feaf4f5a7f593f4efe5950150cbccf14aaf2b22dc7852d6d7a7bc9f","text":"# Preserve SQL Explorer whitespace and reconcile PR #9\n\n## Summary\n\nContinue against pinned dev `5b3b02d1a9c2afa93b6d0d4a1eac7dbfc03b828b`, preserving the complete feature checkpoint and authenticated history.\n\nThe rejected capture’s widget and compositor rows show `SELECT c.c│FROM`: caret rendering replaces the separator space. The saved source already contains the selected whitespace-preserving correction and focused regressions. Preserve that work; the confirmed remaining edit is removal of three changelog conflict markers. No material implementation question remains.\n\n## Implementation and compatibility\n\n- Preserve `analytics_toolkit/sql_explorer/editor.py`’s correction: underline every in-document character, including spaces and all visible expanded-tab cells, for primary and secondary carets. Render vertical bars only in end-of-line or empty-line padding.\n- Preserve underlying SQL, whitespace, foreground/background colors, cell widths, selections, scrolling, ruler alignment and completion behavior. Retain wrapped and horizontally clipped tab handling.\n- Preserve the existing completion scene’s `SELECT c.c FROM` text. Completion must retain its suffix and produce `SELECT c.customer_id FROM…`; the evidence does not justify changing insertion semantics or adding another separator.\n- In `docs/CHANGELOG.md`, remove conflict markers at lines 73, 77 and 88. Retain all three feature-side entries and all ten dev-side entries under Unreleased, preserving historical releases. Check the complete file for additional markers.\n- Preserve the existing concise task fragment and updated caret documentation. Fully read files before editing; retain recovered tests and documentation.\n- Keep public APIs, runtime/test dependencies, Python 3.8–3.14 and supported Textual compatibility unchanged. Preserve supersampling, diagnostics, selected narrow UI repairs, coverage targets and debt baselines.\n\n## Required feature behavior\n\n- Retain anchored Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down selection, independent preferred columns, multiple cursors per row, selection merging, movement, atomic editing/undo/redo, bounded history retention and reset cleanup. Shift+Up/Down toggles only the exact projected position.\n- Retain document-order Ctrl+C/`cp`/Ctrl+X fragments, including empties. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor copies the whole buffer.\n- Retain shared keyboard/command/terminal paste precedence: matching fragments, matching lines while ignoring one trailing line ending, then whole-text repetition. Preserve metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\nPrivate workers execute no programs, tests, installs or rendering. Perform all validation on GitHub.\n\n- Run the existing caret-rendering and completion-spacing regressions first. Require primary/secondary spaces and tabs to retain text, colors and widths in widget and compositor output, with editor and command focus, wrapping and horizontal clipping.\n- Require completion opening to preserve the rendered separator; acceptance must preserve the suffix, cursor position and undo/redo behavior without executing a query. Retain occupied-text underline and end-of-line bar coverage.\n- Run adjacent caret-color, ruler, highlight, multicursor, selection/clipboard, history/reset, completion-readiness, menu, checkbox/selector and capture regressions.\n- Require fresh exact-head lint, format, type, artifact, Python/minimum-dependency, SDK and aggregate checks. Retain canonical coverage JSON and floors of **98.03% branch**, **98.92% combined** and **99.22% statement**, plus subsystem floors.\n- Obtain a trusted isolated capture of the corrected candidate. Independently inspect `completion-columns` and every one of the **46 full PNGs**, requiring all geometry assertions and individual visual verdicts to pass before correction publication. Retain picker comparison evidence.\n- Bind validation to the actual candidate, checkpoint, task, plan, dependency versions and dev base. Published-head successes do not validate saved edits.\n\n## Review, dependencies and completion\n\n- Obtain fresh independent plan review before coding. Revalidate coordinator dependencies and preserve the durable correction barrier; archived recovery receipts grant no current approval or dependent-PR release.\n- Require complete independent implementation review of every diff continuation, including diagnostic/capture modules, tests and companion implementation evidence. Earlier partial reviews remain incomplete.\n- Revalidate changed heads and dev bases. Preserve complete provenance, original questions/answers and planning records, credentials, genuine-input holds, owner vetoes and applicable real-owner exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator must verify the RPi recommendation-policy companion work, independent resolution records, safe activation and recovery of agents waiting solely on routine choices. Preserve security and genuine-input holds.\n- Monitor PR #9, recommendation-policy/restart companion work and every task-related repair PR through successful merges into `dev` and required post-merge validation. Completing this correction alone does not complete that objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"65168e2a36952fea016fd3db3f756554f4bdd454fbf2f12bb23b38f4e2c60478","text":"# Correct primary-caret colors and reconcile PR #9 with dev\n\n## Summary\n\nPreserve the complete feature checkpoint and reconcile against pinned dev `1f7ff62aeba3c27a307a606b80459bca78b2dfd5`.\n\nPublished head `b416cd92b239290298c3e51758fb4c5db143c29a` fails three focused whitespace-caret cases across all eight matrix environments. Its hash-bound completion PNG and widget/compositor diagnostics confirm native block colors beneath the underline. Quality checks also identify formatting in the caret-rendering tests.\n\nThe independent resolver selected **Native styling**. No material implementation question remains; that selection grants no plan, implementation, visual, protected-policy, or merge approval.\n\n## Implementation and compatibility\n\n- In `analytics_toolkit/sql_explorer/editor.py`, replace pre-resolution cursor suppression with a private render-only theme adapter. Delegate Textual CSS resolution to a copied theme, then neutralize its cursor style before native rendering consumes it. Preserve all other resolved styles and restore the original theme in `finally`, including rendering failures. Keep the absent-theme path intact.\n- Preserve the existing underline overlay for every in-document character, space, and visible expanded-tab cell. Keep vertical bars exclusively in end-of-line and empty-line padding. Preserve text, foreground/background colors, widths, selection/search styling, scrolling, ruler mapping, and completion behavior.\n- In `tests/sql/explorer/caret_rendering.py`, retain every existing assertion and apply canonical Ruff formatting. Extend mounted coverage using the actual `TextArea.render_line`, checking syntax-colored text and the `SELECT c.c FROM` separator alongside existing space/tab cases.\n- Reconcile stale automation changes with pinned dev: restore `.github/agent/review_control.py`, `tests/repository/notification_metadata.py`, and `tests/repository/label_reconciliation.py` exactly to the pinned base. Their current differences remove newer notification and provenance safeguards.\n- Reconcile operations documentation using pinned dev’s current contract and source associations. Preserve useful feature-specific activation requirements without reinstating obsolete “staged, not active” claims.\n- Reconcile the changelog using pinned dev’s history plus every distinct feature entry. Remove only conflict markers and exact duplicates; retain historical releases and record this correction through the managed fragment mechanism.\n- Fully read each edited file through its final continuation before writing. Preserve recovered source, documentation, diagnostics, authenticated history, and useful checkpoint changes.\n\nPublic APIs, method signatures, dependencies, Python 3.8–3.14/Textual compatibility, diagnostic interfaces, coverage targets, and debt baselines remain unchanged.\n\n## Feature requirements retained\n\n- Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down extends anchored selections across logical lines without creating cursors. Preserve independent preferred columns, short-line clamping, reversal, multiple cursors per row, selection merging, atomic editing/history, bounded snapshot retention, and reset cleanup. Shift+Up/Down toggles only the exact projected position.\n- Ctrl+C, `cp`, and Ctrl+X retain document-order fragments, including empties. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Keyboard, command, and terminal paste distribute matching fragments first, matching lines second while ignoring one trailing line ending, and otherwise repeat the complete text. Preserve metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Retain the selected narrow UI/fixture repairs, supersampling, bounded comparison evidence, and strict diagnostics. Preserve completion suffixes and existing SQL separators. The inspected picker PNG supplies no reason for another rendering change.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\nPrivate workers execute no programs, tests, installs, or rendering.\n\n- First run caret-rendering, caret-color, render-lifecycle, and completion-spacing regressions on GitHub with minimum/current supported Textual dependencies.\n- Require real widget and compositor output to preserve primary/secondary caret text, colors, and widths under editor and command focus. Cover spaces, expanded tabs, wrapping, horizontal clipping, syntax text, selections, search highlights, and padding bars.\n- Verify original theme identity and state after repeated renders, focus changes, missing styles, absent themes, and native-render exceptions. Preserve existing mocked unit tests alongside real-renderer coverage.\n- Run restored notification/provenance regressions and adjacent multicursor, clipboard, movement/history/reset, ruler, completion, menu, checkbox/selector, and capture suites.\n- Require fresh exact-head lint/format/type, artifact, Python/minimum-dependency matrix, SDK conformance, and aggregate checks. Retain canonical coverage JSON and floors of **98.03% branch**, **98.92% combined**, **99.22% statement**, plus subsystem floors. The failed coverage test run establishes no new coverage shortfall.\n- Obtain a trusted isolated GitHub capture of the corrected candidate. Inspect `completion-columns`, then all **46 full PNGs**, requiring every geometry assertion and individual visual verdict to pass before correction publication. Retain picker comparisons.\n- Bind validation to actual source, checkpoint, candidate, task, plan, dependency versions, and dev base. Published-head evidence does not validate saved edits.\n\n## Review and completion\n\n- Obtain fresh independent plan review before coding and complete independent implementation review afterward, covering every diff continuation and companion implementation evidence.\n- Revalidate changed heads and dev bases. Preserve durable dependency/correction barriers, complete provenance, credentials, genuine-input holds, owner vetoes, and applicable real-owner exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator verifies recommendation-policy companion completion, safe activation, recorded independent resolutions, and recovery of agents waiting solely on routine implementation choices. Historical receipts do not release current holds.\n- Monitor PR #9, recommendation-policy/restart companion work, and every task-related repair PR through successful merges into `dev` and required post-merge validation. This bounded correction does not complete that overall objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"65b765782ecd88e9b234d2c3e237161bb1fbe780dae4e4d6874b6733b527774c","text":"# Correct PR #9’s remaining formatting failure\n\n## Summary\n\nContinue from head `f0f0abc4346f085df2e9058b9613532b04f2c227` against pinned dev `1f7ff62aeba3c27a307a606b80459bca78b2dfd5`.\n\nComplete feedback and failed-job logs identify one blocker: Ruff formatting in `tests/sql/explorer/caret_rendering.py`. Matrix, SDK, type, coverage, and artifact validation passed. The latest exact-head review reports complete source, companion, and 46-scene review without concrete blockers.\n\nNo material implementation question remains.\n\n## Implementation and compatibility\n\n- Apply canonical Ruff 0.15.22 formatting only to `tests/sql/explorer/caret_rendering.py`, using the existing Python 3.8 target, 100-character line length, and LF configuration. Private coding workers make source-only edits; formatting verification runs on GitHub.\n- Preserve every test, parameter combination, fixture value, assertion, and negative control. In particular, retain real native-renderer and compositor checks for syntax colors, whitespace, primary/secondary carets, and original theme restoration.\n- Preserve the complete feature checkpoint and authenticated history. Do not reopen resolved production caret, completion, picker, menu, or controller corrections without new evidence.\n- Record the correction through the managed changelog mechanism, preserving historical entries and package/README versions.\n- Keep public APIs, method signatures, dependencies, Python 3.8–3.14/Textual compatibility, diagnostic schemas, coverage targets, and debt baselines unchanged.\n- Fully read edited files before writing and revalidate against any changed head or dev base.\n\n## Required feature behavior retained\n\n- Preserve anchored Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down selection, independent preferred columns, multiple cursors per row, selection merging, atomic editing/undo/redo, bounded history retention, reset cleanup, and exact-position Shift+Up/Down toggling.\n- Preserve document-order Ctrl+C/`cp`/Ctrl+X fragments, including empties. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Preserve shared keyboard/command/terminal paste precedence: matching fragments, matching lines ignoring one trailing line ending, then whole-text repetition. Retain metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Preserve thin underlines over every in-document character and expanded-tab cell, with original colors and widths. Reserve vertical bars for line-end/empty-line padding.\n- Retain selected narrow UI repairs, supersampled capture, recovered documentation/tests, and bounded diagnostic evidence.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\nAll execution occurs on GitHub; private workers execute no programs, tests, installs, or rendering.\n\n- First verify canonical formatting and lint for the affected module. Require zero new findings without changing baselines.\n- Run its existing regressions alongside caret-color, render-lifecycle, and completion-spacing coverage on minimum/current supported dependencies. No additional tests are needed for formatting alone.\n- Require fresh exact-head quality, Python compatibility/minimum-dependency, SDK, artifact, and aggregate fast checks.\n- Retain canonical coverage JSON and floors of **98.03% branches**, **98.92% combined**, **99.22% statements**, plus subsystem floors. Current passing coverage supplies no reason for additional coverage corrections.\n- Obtain the required candidate-bound GitHub visual capture and independent review of all **46 full PNGs** and geometry results. Retain picker comparisons; prior-head evidence cannot certify the corrected head.\n\n## Review and completion\n\n- Obtain fresh independent plan review before coding and implementation review afterward, confirming the correction preserves assertions and the complete feature.\n- Bind checks, captures, and reviews to the actual source, checkpoint, candidate, dev base, task, plan, and dependencies.\n- Preserve provenance, durable correction/dependency barriers, credentials, genuine-input holds, owner vetoes, and applicable real-owner exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator verifies recommendation-policy companion completion and safe activation, recorded independent resolutions, and recovery of agents waiting solely on routine implementation choices.\n- Continue monitoring PR #9 and all task-related companion/correction PRs through successful merges into `dev` and required post-merge validation. This formatting correction does not complete the broader monitoring objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"dd261ae545b847735e796b558078dd265282511e0f553ceb3fc6c330bfe6bc1a","text":"# Reconcile PR #9 with current dev and complete review\n\n## Summary\n\nPreserve the complete SQL Explorer feature while reconciling with pinned dev `7142aac73dbc26fb0195b61e1dce7bcf8aa19e5a`.\n\nPublished head `ae84e66f77366547be44580cbdd5d5c9f51140bd` has 12 passing non-review checks and a final receipt recording 46 scene passes against the previous base. Independent whole-feature review remains incomplete. Those results do not validate the forthcoming reconciliation.\n\nThe recorded answer selects **Preserve dev safeguards**. No material implementation question remains.\n\n## Implementation changes\n\n- Restore these files byte-for-byte from immutable pinned dev:\n  - `.github/agent/capture_artifact.py`\n  - `.github/workflows/agent-visual.yml`\n  - `tests/repository/capture_artifact.py`\n  - `agent_tools/task_evidence/1253260b20f14ee680edd15d01547757/parent-objective.json`\n- In `docs/GITHUB_AGENT_OPERATIONS.md`, retain all pinned-dev content, including failed-capture export limits and authority boundaries, plus the feature-specific recommendation-policy activation section.\n- Reconcile `docs/CHANGELOG.md` using pinned dev’s history and every distinct feature entry. Restore the five removed dev entries; remove only conflict markers and exact duplicates. Preserve historical releases and package/README versions.\n- Fully read each affected file through its final continuation before editing. Preserve recovered tests, diagnostic helpers, documentation, authenticated history and existing useful checkpoint changes.\n- Make no speculative editor, clipboard, UI or rendering corrections. Any newly demonstrated defect requires a concrete finding, focused regression and renewed independently reviewed correction plan.\n\n## Feature and compatibility requirements\n\n- Preserve anchored Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down selection, independent preferred columns, multiple cursors per row, selection merging, atomic editing/undo/redo, bounded history retention and reset cleanup. Shift+Up/Down toggles only the exact projected position.\n- Preserve document-order fragments for Ctrl+C, `cp` and Ctrl+X, including empties. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Preserve shared keyboard/command/terminal paste precedence: matching fragments, matching lines ignoring one trailing line ending, then whole-text repetition. Retain metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Preserve thin underlines over every in-document character and expanded-tab cell, retaining text, colors and widths. Reserve vertical bars for line-end and empty-line padding.\n- Retain selected narrow UI repairs, completion suffixes, supersampling and bounded diagnostic comparisons.\n- Public APIs, method signatures, dependency declarations, diagnostic interfaces and Python 3.8–3.14/Textual compatibility remain unchanged.\n\n## Focused coverage and GitHub validation\n\nPrivate workers execute no programs, tests, installs or rendering.\n\n- Verify restored files match pinned-dev hashes and that documentation/changelog retain both dev and feature content.\n- Run restored capture-exporter regressions first on GitHub, retaining unsafe-path, changed-file, capacity, partial-evidence and failed-capture controls. Reuse existing tests; add tests only for a demonstrated uncovered failure.\n- Run focused multicursor, selection/clipboard, history/reset, native-renderer caret, completion-spacing, menu-viewport, checkbox/selector and capture-diagnostics regressions.\n- Require fresh exact-head quality, type, artifact, Python/minimum-dependency matrix, SDK and aggregate fast checks. Retain canonical coverage JSON and existing floors: **98.03% branch**, **98.92% combined**, **99.22% statement**, plus subsystem and debt baselines.\n- Obtain a trusted isolated GitHub capture of the reconciled candidate at 208×47 cells and 1280×800 pixels. Require every geometry assertion and individual full-PNG verdict for all **46 scenes**; retain picker comparisons.\n- Bind all evidence to the actual candidate, checkpoint, task, plan, dependencies and current dev base. Earlier capture-stage pending fields do not invalidate the predecessor’s final receipt, but that receipt cannot certify new content.\n\n## Independent review and completion\n\n- Obtain fresh current-base plan review before coding, followed by complete independent implementation review.\n- Assess every diff continuation, explicitly including `tests/agent_tools/render_diagnostics.py`, `svg_evidence.py`, `visual_lifecycle.py`, associated helpers and capture integration. Track assessed ranges separately from retrieved pages.\n- Complete companion source/test assessment and verify exact-commit CI, installed-source identity, activation, rollback and waiting-agent recovery evidence. Preserve genuine-input and security holds.\n- Preserve review progress and evidence across retries. Incomplete assessment must remain a review-routing issue; it supplies no product defect or correction approval.\n- Preserve provenance, dependency barriers, credentials, owner vetoes and applicable real-owner exact-head protected approvals. The reconciliation choice grants none of these approvals.\n- After complete independent approval and required gates, use the trusted merge workflow. Continue coordinator monitoring of PR #9, recommendation-policy/restart companion work and every task-related repair PR until all merge successfully into `dev` and required post-merge validation completes.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"ab2679dc24629062eb4499ec69be0ecedf4768a71b27496b508cfb6baf84cd40","text":"# Preserve SQL Explorer and validate the saved diagnostic checkpoint\n\n## Summary\n\nContinue against pinned dev `7142aac73dbc26fb0195b61e1dce7bcf8aa19e5a`, preserving the complete feature and authenticated history.\n\nPublished head `98508973146e4137a88eaacff9a4cc13f8e84d9c` has passing non-review checks but a rejected visual review. The inspected PNG shows separate ruler and gutter labels; secondary-caret visibility remains unresolved. Its geometry lacks the diagnostics now present in the saved checkpoint.\n\nThe recorded **Preserve ruler** and **Diagnose first** choices settle the approach. No material question remains unanswered.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Remove only the extra blank line at EOF in `tests/agent_tools/multicursor_diagnostics.py`, retaining one terminating newline and every test, fixture and assertion.\n- Preserve the saved caret diagnostics in `agent_tools/sql_explorer_render_diagnostics.py`: actual selections, primary identity, preferred columns, focus, keyboard mode, scrolling, viewport and terminal-cell mapping; exact widget/compositor text, colors and style flags. Keep expected fixture state separate from observations.\n- Preserve single-export integration in `agent_tools/sql_explorer_visual_capture.py`: retain exact raw, framed and supersampling SVG inputs, ordinary PNG hashes, renderer settings and processing metadata through atomic geometry JSON publication.\n- Retain existing bounds: nine regions/carets, 24 rows, 208 cells, 256 parsed SVG elements, 512 KiB reduced diagnostics and 4 MiB combined lossless SVG inputs. Missing probes, clipping, limits and failures must explicitly identify incomplete evidence.\n- Preserve the mounted tab/database-switch ruler regression and scene metadata distinguishing the active-column label from the first gutter/text row. Retain overlap, shifted-mapping and missing-label negative controls.\n- Preserve current-dev capture safeguards, recovered source/documentation, selected narrow UI repairs, supersampling and picker comparisons. Retain the managed changelog fragment without changing package versions.\n- Keep collection observational: no new refocusing, event draining, retries, timing changes, scene-state correction or production/export presentation changes.\n\nPublic APIs, signatures, dependencies and Python 3.8–3.14/Textual compatibility remain unchanged. Diagnostic JSON additions remain additive.\n\n## Feature requirements retained\n\n- Anchored Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down selection without spawning cursors; independent preferred columns, reversal, short-line clamping and boundaries.\n- Multiple cursors per row, selection merging, independent movement/editing, atomic undo/redo, bounded history and reset cleanup. Shift+Up/Down toggles only the exact projected position.\n- Document-order Ctrl+C/`cp`/Ctrl+X fragments, including empties. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor copies the whole buffer.\n- Shared keyboard/command/terminal paste precedence: matching fragments, matching lines ignoring one trailing line ending, then whole-text repetition. Preserve metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Thin primary/secondary carets preserving SQL, whitespace, expanded tabs, colors, widths and mapping: underlines in every in-document cell; bars only in line-end or empty-line padding.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\nPrivate workers execute no programs, tests, installs or rendering.\n\n- Obtain fresh independent plan review before source correction.\n- On GitHub, first check formatting and run the existing multicursor-diagnostics, ruler, visual-state and capture-lifecycle regressions. Verify collection preserves state and distinguishes missing evidence from observed absent caret marks.\n- Retain Unicode, combining-character, wide-cell, expanded-tab, clipping, unavailable-compositor, limit, single-export, atomic-publication and readiness/geometry rejection coverage.\n- Run focused multicursor, selection/clipboard, history/reset, native-renderer caret and completion regressions, followed by required quality, type, artifact, compatibility/minimum-dependency, SDK and aggregate checks.\n- Retain canonical coverage JSON and floors of **98.03% branches**, **98.92% combined** and **99.22% statements**, plus subsystem floors and debt baselines.\n- Use the trusted temporary-candidate GitHub capture route. Bind evidence to actual source, checkpoint, candidate, base, task, plan, dependencies and run; verify extracted SVG and PNG hashes.\n- Independently inspect the new caret layers and full PNG to identify the first failing layer. Recorded underline styles alone cannot establish visibility. Inconclusive observations remain unresolved; a demonstrated production/export repair requires renewed independent planning.\n- Submit the ruler evidence for independent reassessment while retaining the current rejection. Require all **46** geometry checks and individual full-PNG verdicts before correction publication.\n\n## Review and completion\n\n- Complete independent assessment of every feature diff continuation, diagnostic/capture module, associated test and companion implementation. Track assessed ranges separately from retrieved pages.\n- Revalidate changed heads and dev bases. Preserve complete provenance, dependency barriers, credentials, genuine-input holds, owner vetoes and applicable real-owner exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator verifies recommendation-policy companion completion, recorded independent resolutions, safe activation and recovery of agents waiting solely on routine choices. Preserve frozen rollout sources and completed deployments.\n- Monitor PR #9, the recommendation-policy/restart companion work and every task-related repair PR through successful merges into `dev` and required post-merge validation. This diagnostic checkpoint does not complete that overall objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"ba2ca6de6e000df75238880cfd1237b0f8fb42b4d83747a5e9cacaf901396d87","text":"# Preserve SQL Explorer and validate the correction checkpoint\n\n## Summary\n\nContinue against pinned dev `7142aac73dbc26fb0195b61e1dce7bcf8aa19e5a`, preserving the complete feature, useful saved edits, recovered source/documentation, and authenticated task history.\n\nComplete assigned feedback binds failed CI and visual rejection to published head `43852778725dc1bb13b91b7a735cafaf9bacf5f6`. It does not validate unpublished checkpoint changes.\n\nThe recorded **Narrow gate repairs** and **Faithful diagnostics** choices settle this correction sequence. No material owner question remains. First validate the saved journal correction and faithful diagnostics; use fresh GitHub evidence before selecting remaining presentation, export, focus, or layout repairs.\n\n## Implementation changes\n\n- Preserve the saved correction in `analytics_toolkit/sql_explorer/journal_screen.py`: empty failed reads show the warning alone; successful empty reads show “No matching journal entries.” Populated pages retain their count and any warning. Preserve stale-generation rejection, recovery, controls, and query behavior.\n- Preserve `agent_tools/sql_explorer_render_diagnostics.py`’s cell-based cropping: retain combining suffixes with a completely retained base, including across differently styled spans; preserve original colors/styles and expanded-tab cells; represent partially clipped wide cells faithfully without mutating observations.\n- Retain saved fixes for test-variable shadowing, compound assertions, long lines, formatting, and scene-collector complexity. Preserve every assertion, negative control, fixture value, diagnostic ordering, and failure-containment behavior. Do not add suppressions or change debt baselines.\n- Preserve the added command-caret and new-file diagnostics, associated scene/capture integration, and ruler lifecycle snapshots. Record actual focus, selections, preferred columns, scroll, cell mapping, widget/compositor rows and styles, screen ancestry, resolved alignment, geometry, pending layout flags, queue sizes, row lengths, and dependency versions.\n- Keep observations bounded: nine regions/carets, 24 rows, 208 cells, 256 parsed SVG elements, 512 KiB reduced diagnostics, 8 KiB lifecycle snapshots, and existing lossless SVG/comparison budgets. Explicitly identify unavailable, clipped, omitted, or incomplete evidence.\n- Preserve single-export ownership, exact raw/framed/supersampling SVG inputs, PNG hashes, renderer settings, and atomic geometry publication through the existing artifact route. Do not refocus, drain queues, retry assertions, alter timing, or force scene state.\n- Retain the managed changelog fragment and current-dev capture/provenance safeguards. Fully read affected files through their final continuation before any subsequent edit.\n\nPublic APIs, method signatures, dependencies, diagnostic compatibility, and Python 3.8–3.14/Textual support remain unchanged. Diagnostic additions are additive.\n\n## Complete feature requirements retained\n\n- Anchored Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down selection without spawning cursors; independent preferred columns, short-line clamping, reversal, and boundaries.\n- Independent multicursor movement/editing, multiple cursors per row, selection merging, exact-position Shift+Up/Down toggling, atomic undo/redo, bounded history metadata, and reset cleanup.\n- Document-order Ctrl+C/`cp`/Ctrl+X fragments, including empties. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Shared keyboard/command/terminal paste precedence: matching fragments, matching lines while ignoring one trailing line ending, then whole-text repetition. Preserve metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Thin primary/secondary underlines over all in-document characters, spaces, and expanded-tab cells; bars only in line-end/empty-line padding. Preserve SQL, colors, widths, selection/scroll/ruler mapping, and completion suffixes.\n- Preserve the selected narrow UI/fixture repairs, ruler presentation/reassessment, picker correction, supersampling, comparison evidence, and recovered tests/documentation. Partial implementation supplies no additional scope.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub evidence\n\nPrivate workers execute no programs, tests, installs, or rendering.\n\n1. Obtain fresh independent whole-plan review before coding.\n2. On GitHub, first run diagnostic lint/format checks and the existing multicursor-diagnostics, scene-observations, ruler/visual-state, and journal-status regressions.\n3. Require Unicode, cross-span combining marks, wide-cell clipping, expanded tabs, style preservation, missing compositor, bounds, unavailable probes, non-mutation, journal failure/recovery, and stale-result controls to pass.\n4. Retain the strict ruler focus and widget/compositor equality assertions. Capture their original failing-state snapshots without recollection. Obtain exact-candidate GitHub observations before changing focus, widths, assertions, or lifecycle behavior.\n5. Capture command-caret, keyboard-multicursor, and new-file scenes with the saved diagnostics. Independently compare widget, compositor, SVG, and full PNG layers. Recorded underline flags alone do not establish visible carets. New-file alignment must be traced through actual resolved screen/dialog layout before selecting its repair.\n6. Run adjacent selection/clipboard, history/reset, native-renderer caret, completion, menu, checkbox/selector, SVG-evidence, supersampling, capture-lifecycle, and restored safeguard regressions.\n7. Require exact-head quality/type, artifact, compatibility/minimum-dependency matrix, SDK, and aggregate fast checks. Retain canonical coverage JSON, **98.03% branch**, **98.92% combined**, **99.22% statement**, subsystem floors, and debt baselines. Failed tests establish no new coverage shortfall.\n\nBind all observations to actual source, checkpoint, candidate, base, task, plan, dependencies, GitHub run, and artifact hashes. Inconclusive evidence remains unresolved. Any demonstrated remaining repair requires a concrete renewed plan and independent review.\n\n## Review, publication, and completion\n\n- Keep existing visual rejections in force. After reviewed repairs, obtain fresh independent complete-feature/source review and all **46** candidate-bound geometry checks and individual full **1280×800 PNG** verdicts at the **208×47** terminal grid. Historical captures cannot certify new edits.\n- Assess every diff continuation and companion implementation; track assessed coverage separately from retrieved pages. Revalidate changed heads and dev bases.\n- Preserve complete provenance, credentials, genuine-input/security holds, owner veto/cancel, dependency barriers—including PR #10’s actual PR #9 ancestry—and applicable real-owner exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator verifies recommendation-policy/restart/recovery, producer-consumer/exporter compatibility, activation and rollback evidence. Preserve frozen rollout sources, completed deployments, notification limits, concurrency 10, truthful lifecycle labels, authenticated responses, the single 30-minute/open-PR orchestrator, idle exit, and coordinator-owned drain pause.\n- Use trusted publication and merge mechanisms only after required gates. Continue coordinator monitoring and aligned repairs for PR #9, the recommendation-policy/restart companion work, and every qualifying repair PR through successful `dev` merges and required post-merge validation. This diagnostic checkpoint does not complete that objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"a7052639e6cfc2694f714789db06ed529351f2900652de1bbba7dac4277eacb6","text":"# Preserve SQL Explorer and trace the remaining ruler failures\n\n## Summary\n\nContinue from published head `c1976299ef64679a9e1335825800277a3c6e9f15` against pinned dev `f66a80ebe4b3c28dbca17fbc58c2d6ffe464bb01`.\n\nApply the selected **Trace lifecycle** sequence: correct confirmed lint/format findings, restore inherited dev safeguards, and collect bounded GitHub evidence before choosing a focus or row-width repair. No material implementation question remains for this diagnostic checkpoint.\n\nCurrent logs establish unexpected editor focus and, on Textual 0.89.1, 205 widget cells versus 206 compositor cells. They do not establish callback execution order or the first padding divergence.\n\n## Implementation changes\n\n- In `agent_tools/sql_explorer_render_diagnostics.py`, refactor `_targets` to assign the selected target list and return once. Preserve lazy scene-specific queries, target order, requested row counts, filtering, exceptions and diagnostic output. Resolve `PLR0911` without suppressions.\n- Apply canonical repository Ruff formatting to `tests/agent_tools/multicursor_diagnostics.py`. Preserve every fixture, assertion, parameter and Unicode/style negative control.\n- Add test-support instrumentation around the existing ruler regression and visual scene. Record callback scheduling and execution order for tab activation, database switching and deferred focus restoration; include active tab, focused-widget identity and remembered-focus identity before and after each observed callback.\n- Invoke each wrapped callback exactly once with its original arguments, return value and exception behavior. Preserve its scheduler and execution position. Install instrumentation before scene configuration and restore wrappers during cleanup; change no production tab/workspace behavior.\n- Extend ruler observations with original strip cell/character lengths, requested crop width, resulting lengths, region/content widths, scrollbar/gutter state and exact trailing text/style spans. Observe the strips already collected for that snapshot; do not pad, trim, rerender or normalize them.\n- Bound the lifecycle trace to 64 events and 8 KiB. Report overflow, unavailable probes and collection failures explicitly. Preserve the first failing snapshot alongside its trace; diagnostics must not replace the original assertion failure.\n- Retain exact focus and widget/compositor equality assertions, geometry checks and negative controls. Add no refocusing, sleeps, queue draining, retries or scene-state changes.\n- Restore `.github/agent/review_control.py` and the deleted `tests/repository/coordinator_scope.py` byte-for-byte from pinned dev. Retain dev’s coordinator-scope documentation plus the feature-specific activation section. Restore the three removed dev changelog entries while preserving all distinct feature entries and historical releases.\n- Fully read edited files through their final continuation before writing. Preserve recovered source/documentation and the useful checkpoint; record this correction through the managed changelog mechanism without changing package versions.\n\nPublic APIs, method signatures, dependencies and Python 3.8–3.14/Textual compatibility remain unchanged. Diagnostic fields are additive; existing fields and budgets retain their meaning.\n\n## Complete feature contract retained\n\n- Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down extends anchored selections across logical lines without creating cursors, preserving independent preferred columns through short lines, reversal and boundaries.\n- Preserve independent and same-row multicursors, selection merging, exact-position Shift+Up/Down toggles, atomic editing/undo/redo, bounded history metadata and document-reset cleanup.\n- Ctrl+C, `cp` and Ctrl+X retain document-order fragments, including empties. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Keyboard, command and terminal paste use matching fragments first, matching lines second while ignoring one trailing line ending, then whole-text repetition. Preserve metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Preserve thin primary/secondary underlines over text, spaces and expanded tabs; bars appear only in padding. Preserve SQL, colors, widths, selections, scrolling, ruler mapping and completion suffixes.\n- Retain selected narrow UI/fixture repairs, journal failure reporting, faithful combining-mark/style cropping, supersampling and lossless capture evidence. Remaining command-caret, ruler and new-file findings stay unresolved until fresh evidence supports a reviewed correction.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub evidence\n\nAll execution occurs on GitHub. Private workers execute no programs, tests, installs or rendering.\n\n- Test trace ordering, bounded retention, unavailable probes, cleanup and faithful forwarding of callback results/exceptions. Verify instrumentation preserves focus, text, selections, preferences, scroll and callback execution counts.\n- Test strip observations with unequal widths, trailing spaces, styled padding, combining marks and wide cells. Require recorded original bytes/styles and lengths to survive unchanged.\n- Run the instrumented ruler regression first on canonical Python 3.11/Textual 0.73.0 and Python 3.14/Textual 0.89.1, then the supported matrix. Retain expected failures and their original snapshots; diagnostic success does not require making the regression pass.\n- Run restored coordinator-scope regressions, adjacent ruler/scene observations, multicursor diagnostics, journal-status and capture-lifecycle tests. Follow with focused selection/clipboard, history/reset, native caret, completion, menu, checkbox/selector and SVG/supersampling regressions.\n- Require exact-head lint/format/type, artifact, compatibility/minimum-dependency, SDK and aggregate checks. Retain canonical coverage JSON and floors of **98.03% branch**, **98.92% combined**, **99.22% statement**, plus subsystem floors and debt baselines. Failed tests establish no new coverage shortfall.\n- Use the existing trusted temporary-candidate route and artifact transport. Bind observations to actual source, checkpoint, candidate, base, task, plan, dependency versions, run and hashes. Preserve single-export ownership and atomic evidence publication.\n\nAfter independently assessing the new lifecycle, strip, command-caret and dialog evidence, produce a separate concrete repair plan for each demonstrated remaining cause. Inconclusive evidence remains unresolved.\n\n## Review and completion\n\n- Obtain fresh independent review of this complete current-base plan before coding, followed by independent implementation review. Revalidate changed heads or dev bases.\n- Keep visual rejections in force. Before correction publication, require complete feature/source review and all **46** geometry checks and individual full **1280×800 PNG** verdicts at **208×47** cells. Historical captures cannot certify new edits.\n- Preserve complete authenticated history, question/options/answer records, provenance, credentials, owner veto/cancel, dependency barriers—including PR #10’s actual PR #9 ancestry—and applicable exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator retains companion recommendation-policy/restart/recovery, producer-consumer/exporter compatibility and activation/rollback verification. Preserve notification limits, concurrency 10, truthful lifecycle labels, authenticated responses and the single 30-minute/open-PR orchestrator with idle exit. Honor actual current runtime holds; historical pause statements neither establish nor release one. Preserve frozen rollout sources and completed deployments.\n- Continue coordinator monitoring and aligned repairs for PR #9 and every qualifying companion/correction PR through successful `dev` merges and required post-merge validation. This diagnostic checkpoint does not complete that broader objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"243f9516de3a3cfd3dd817a81b491c72c30fcfcfc68c2c426fdcdee3e8488b3e","text":"# Correct the SQL Explorer harness and preserve the complete feature\n\n## Summary\n\nContinue from head `f04d007c090bff62a19a6c2adb7f91bc242d3ecc` against pinned dev `f66a80ebe4b3c28dbca17fbc58c2d6ffe464bb01`.\n\nImplement the recorded **Correct harness layers** choice. Current GitHub evidence identifies deferred focus restoration overriding scene initialization, and a comparison between raw widget output and styled compositor output. Correct those harness boundaries and the confirmed lint findings. Preserve production tab restoration and ruler presentation.\n\nNo material implementation question remains. The selected strategy supplies no plan, source, visual, protected-policy, or merge approval.\n\n## Implementation changes\n\n- **Order scene initialization** in `agent_tools/sql_explorer_visual_scene.py`. Keep `tab-database-change` unconfigured until initialization finishes. Activate the target workspace and switch its database once. Use a scene-only, one-shot continuation after the real deferred restoration callback and its queued focus application; then request command focus once. Mark initialization complete through a subsequent queued continuation after that focus application. Delegate production restoration unchanged and exactly once.\n- Make readiness observe the intended active workspace, database and command focus. Lost focus must invalidate readiness without refocusing. Preserve existing capture rejection and first-failure evidence. Add no sleeps, arbitrary queue draining, assertion retries or repeated corrective focus requests.\n- **Compare equivalent rendering layers.** Preserve existing `widget_row` and raw-strip observations with their original meaning. Add an explicitly named styled widget row from native `render_lines`, using the widget-local content-region clip and mapping it once to screen coordinates. Compare it strictly with the corresponding compositor crop.\n- Require equal complete text, cell lengths and resolved foreground/background/style flags for styled-widget versus compositor rows. Preserve raw-versus-`render_line` fidelity assertions, exact trailing whitespace, original segments and lengths. Do not manufacture padding, trim whitespace or change ruler output to satisfy equality.\n- Keep diagnostic additions compatible and bounded in `agent_tools/sql_explorer_render_diagnostics.py`. Preserve existing limits, unavailable/incomplete reporting, first-failure snapshots, single-export ownership and atomic publication.\n- **Correct confirmed quality findings:** format `agent_tools/sql_explorer_lifecycle_trace.py` and `tests/agent_tools/multicursor_diagnostics.py`; resolve their E501 findings without changing output or fixture bytes. Extract cohesive assertion groups from the ruler regression to resolve PLR0915, preserving every assertion and negative control.\n- Update the diagnostic documentation to distinguish raw, styled-widget and compositor layers and explain ordered initialization. Record a concise managed changelog fragment; preserve historical documentation and release entries. Fully read each edited file through its final continuation before writing.\n\nPublic package APIs, production method signatures, dependencies and Python 3.8–3.14/Textual compatibility remain unchanged. Diagnostic fields are additive.\n\n## Complete feature contract retained\n\n- Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down extends anchored selections across logical lines without spawning cursors, preserving independent preferred columns, reversal, short-line clamping and boundaries.\n- Preserve independent and same-row multicursors, selection merging, exact-position Shift+Up/Down toggles, atomic editing/undo/redo, bounded history metadata and reset cleanup.\n- Ctrl+C, `cp` and Ctrl+X retain document-order fragments, including empties. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Keyboard, command and terminal paste use matching fragments first, matching lines second while ignoring one trailing line ending, then whole-text repetition. Preserve clipboard invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Preserve visible thin primary/secondary underlines over text, spaces and expanded tabs, with bars only in padding. Retain SQL, colors, widths, selection/scroll/ruler mapping and completion suffixes.\n- Preserve selected narrow UI/fixture repairs, journal status correction, supersampling, faithful Unicode/style diagnostics, recovered source/docs and current-dev safeguards. Command-caret, secondary-caret and new-file findings remain unresolved until actual candidate evidence supports independent acceptance or a separately reviewed repair.\n\n## Focused regressions and GitHub validation\n\nAll programs, tests, installs and rendering execute on GitHub.\n\n- Extend the mounted ruler/visual-state regression to prove restoration, queued editor focus, one command-focus request and readiness occur in order. Verify collection preserves focus, text, selections, preferred columns and scroll.\n- Retain independent production tab-focus restoration coverage. Test that later focus loss rejects readiness without another focus request.\n- Test native styled-row/compositor equality across Textual 0.73.0 and 0.89.1, including trailing padding, nonzero origins, gutters, borders and clipping. Preserve raw-strip fidelity, combining marks, wide cells and styles.\n- Retain overlap, shifted mapping, missing-label and missing-gutter controls; extend controls to detect lost trailing cells and incorrect styled-layer colors or flags.\n- First run affected diagnostic, ruler-trace and visual-state modules on canonical Python 3.11 and Python 3.13/3.14 environments, then the supported matrix. Run adjacent multicursor, selection/clipboard, history/reset, caret, completion, journal, menu, checkbox/selector and capture regressions.\n- Require fresh exact-head lint/format/type, artifact, compatibility/minimum-dependency, SDK and aggregate fast checks. Retain canonical coverage JSON and floors of **98.03% branch**, **98.92% combined**, **99.22% statement**, plus subsystem floors and debt baselines. Current failed tests establish no new coverage shortfall.\n- Obtain trusted candidate captures and independently inspect the remaining caret/dialog layers and every one of the **46 full 1280×800 PNGs**, with all geometry checks at **208×47 cells**. Bind evidence to source, checkpoint, candidate, base, task, plan, dependencies, run and hashes. Historical captures cannot validate these edits.\n\n## Review and completion\n\n- Obtain fresh independent review of this complete plan before coding, followed by complete feature/source and visual review. Assess every diff continuation and companion implementation; distinguish retrieved pages from assessed coverage.\n- Keep existing visual rejections effective until fresh independent review resolves them. Contradictory or inconclusive evidence requires renewed planning, never a forced pass.\n- Preserve complete authenticated history, question/options/answer records, credentials, provenance, owner veto/cancel, actual operational holds, dependency barriers—including PR #10’s actual PR #9 ancestry—and applicable exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator verifies recommendation-policy/restart/recovery, producer-consumer/exporter compatibility and activation/rollback evidence. Preserve frozen rollout bytes, completed deployments, notification limits, concurrency 10, truthful lifecycle labels including `agent:writing`, authenticated responses and the single 30-minute/open-PR orchestrator with idle exit. Historical pause records neither establish nor release a current hold.\n- Continue coordinator monitoring and aligned repairs for PR #9, recommendation-policy companions and every qualifying correction PR through successful `dev` merges and required post-merge validation. This harness correction alone does not complete that objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"a302bef0fb4a29e56cbd7c361d9212f7e8251bf94a8111d0a2c74e4fa738eab0","text":"# Correct PR #9’s quality failures and preserve the complete feature\n\n## Summary\n\nContinue from head `813432a565124a7f569c38cb6556757ff58cad24` against pinned dev `f66a80ebe4b3c28dbca17fbc58c2d6ffe464bb01`.\n\nComplete current-head records identify two quality failures: import ordering and test formatting. Python matrix, SDK, type, coverage and artifact validation passed. Historical visual findings remain subject to fresh independent review; their older commit associations do not establish current acceptance.\n\nNo material implementation question remains.\n\n## Implementation changes\n\n- In `tests/agent_tools/styled_rows.py`, correct I001 by moving the `SqlExplorerApp` import into the repository first-party import group, after the `agent_tools` imports. Preserve imported symbols and test behavior.\n- Apply canonical Ruff **0.15.22** formatting to `tests/agent_tools/multicursor_diagnostics.py`, following the existing Python 3.8 target, 100-character line length and LF configuration. Private workers make source-only edits; verification executes on GitHub.\n- Preserve every test, parameter, assertion, negative control, Unicode fixture, style expectation and diagnostic bound. Add no suppressions, skips or baseline changes.\n- Retain the complete saved checkpoint, recovered source/documentation and chronological task records. Fully read affected files before editing; record the correction through the managed changelog mechanism without changing package or README versions.\n- Preserve public APIs, production behavior, dependencies, diagnostic schemas and Python 3.8–3.14/Textual compatibility.\n\n## Complete feature contract retained\n\n- Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down extends anchored selections across logical lines without adding cursors, preserving independent preferred columns, reversal, clamping and boundaries.\n- Retain independent and same-row multicursors, selection merging, exact-position Shift+Up/Down toggles, atomic editing/undo/redo, bounded history metadata and reset cleanup.\n- Ctrl+C, `cp` and Ctrl+X record document-order fragments, including empties. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Keyboard, command and terminal paste use matching fragments first, matching lines second while ignoring one trailing line ending, then whole-text repetition. Preserve metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Preserve visible primary/secondary underlines over text, spaces and expanded tabs, with bars only in padding. Retain SQL, colors, widths, selections, scrolling, ruler mapping and completion suffixes.\n- Preserve selected narrow UI/fixture/journal repairs, supersampling, capture safeguards and faithful diagnostics. Retain ordered scene initialization, raw-strip fidelity and strict native-styled-widget/compositor comparisons. This quality correction introduces no additional presentation repair.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\nAll programs, tests, installs and rendering execute on GitHub.\n\n- First verify import ordering and formatting in the two affected modules, then run the repository quality-debt gate without changing its baselines.\n- Run both existing modules across Textual 0.73.0 and 0.89.1. Retain combining-mark, wide-cell, clipping, trailing-cell, color/style, unavailable-evidence and non-mutation controls, plus production tab-focus restoration coverage. Formatting alone needs no new tests.\n- Run adjacent ruler-trace, visual-state and capture-lifecycle regressions, followed by focused selection/multicursor, clipboard, history/reset, caret and completion coverage.\n- Require fresh final-head lint/format/type, artifact, Python/minimum-dependency matrix, SDK and aggregate fast checks. Retain canonical coverage JSON and existing floors: **98.03% branch, 98.92% combined and 99.22% statement**, plus subsystem floors and debt baselines.\n- Obtain trusted isolated candidate captures at **208×47 cells** and **1280×800 pixels**. Require all **46 geometry checks and individual full-PNG verdicts**, including reassessment of ruler, caret and new-file findings. Preserve picker comparisons and first-failure diagnostics.\n- Bind checks and artifacts to actual source, checkpoint, candidate, base, task, plan, dependencies, run and hashes. Inconclusive findings remain unresolved; demonstrated further repairs require renewed independent planning.\n\n## Review and completion\n\n- Obtain fresh independent whole-plan review before coding, then complete independent feature/source and visual review. Review every diff continuation and companion implementation; retrieved pages alone do not establish assessed coverage.\n- Preserve current-dev safeguards, authenticated history, credentials, owner veto/cancel, actual operational holds, dependency barriers—including PR #10’s actual PR #9 ancestry—and applicable exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator verifies recommendation-policy/restart/recovery and exporter compatibility, activation and rollback evidence. Preserve frozen rollout sources, completed deployments, notification limits, concurrency 10, truthful lifecycle labels, authenticated responses and the single 30-minute/open-PR orchestrator with idle exit.\n- Continue coordinator monitoring and aligned repairs for PR #9, recommendation-policy companions and every qualifying correction PR through successful `dev` merges and required post-merge validation. This formatting correction does not complete that broader objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"d5a4eb2671dc5a311130ec334a76d39678815f9a1e45b289b3f18673e8418a27","text":"# Correct PR #9’s Ruff failures and retain the complete feature\n\n## Summary\n\nContinue from head `75df835553c7281482c3c66c9ca6a9d94e6fdc83` against pinned dev `f66a80ebe4b3c28dbca17fbc58c2d6ffe464bb01`.\n\nRun `39125605452` identifies three blockers: I001 import ordering, one E501 line, and formatting. Type, coverage, artifacts, Python matrix and SDK checks passed. No material implementation question remains. Historical review findings retain their original commit associations and do not establish current acceptance.\n\n## Implementation and compatibility\n\n- In `tests/agent_tools/styled_rows.py`, move the `SqlExplorerApp` import immediately after `import pytest`, before the Rich imports. Preserve the separate `agent_tools` group and every imported symbol.\n- In `tests/agent_tools/multicursor_diagnostics.py`, split the line-209 expected findings list across lines, retaining the exact f-string and assertion. Apply canonical Ruff 0.15.22 formatting using the existing Python 3.8 target, 100-character limit and LF configuration.\n- Preserve every test, parameter, Unicode fixture, assertion, negative control and diagnostic bound. Add no suppressions, skips or baseline changes. Formatting alone requires no new tests.\n- Preserve the entire useful checkpoint, recovered source/documentation and authenticated task history. Record a concise managed changelog fragment without changing package or README versions.\n- Public APIs, production behavior, dependencies, diagnostic schemas and Python 3.8–3.14/Textual compatibility remain unchanged. Fully read affected files before editing; reassess changed heads or dev bases.\n\n## Feature contract retained\n\n- Anchored Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down selection without new cursors; independent preferred columns, same-row multicursors, merging, movement, exact-position Shift+Up/Down toggles, atomic editing/history, bounded metadata and reset cleanup.\n- Document-order Ctrl+C/`cp`/Ctrl+X fragments, including empties; entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing. One unselected cursor copies the whole buffer.\n- Shared keyboard/command/terminal paste precedence: matching fragments, matching lines ignoring one trailing line ending, then whole-text repetition. Preserve metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Thin primary/secondary underlines over in-document text, spaces and expanded tabs; bars only in padding. Preserve SQL, colors, widths, selections, scrolling, ruler mapping and completion.\n- Preserve selected narrow UI/fixture/journal repairs, supersampling, current-dev safeguards, faithful diagnostics, ordered scene initialization, raw-strip fidelity and strict native-styled-widget/compositor comparisons.\n\n## Focused coverage and GitHub validation\n\nAll programs, tests, installs and rendering execute on GitHub; private workers perform source-only work.\n\n- First verify Ruff lint and formatting for both affected modules, then the repository quality-debt gate.\n- Run both existing modules across Textual 0.73.0 and 0.89.1. Retain Unicode/style/clipping/trailing-cell controls, unavailable-evidence reporting, observation non-mutation and production tab-focus restoration coverage.\n- Run adjacent ruler-trace, visual-state and capture-lifecycle regressions, followed by focused selection/multicursor, clipboard, history/reset, caret and completion tests.\n- Require fresh final-head quality/type, artifact, compatibility/minimum-dependency, SDK and aggregate fast checks. Retain canonical coverage JSON and floors of **98.03% branch, 98.92% combined and 99.22% statement**, plus subsystem and debt baselines.\n- Obtain trusted isolated captures at **208×47 cells**, retaining all **46 geometry results and individual full 1280×800 PNG verdicts**, picker comparisons and first-failure evidence. Reassess outstanding ruler, caret and dialog findings independently.\n- Bind evidence to source, checkpoint, candidate, base, task, plan, dependencies, run and hashes. Inconclusive findings remain unresolved; further substantive repairs require renewed independent planning.\n\n## Review and completion\n\n- Obtain fresh independent complete-plan review before coding, followed by complete feature/source, companion and visual review. Track assessed diff coverage separately from retrieved pages.\n- Preserve provenance, credentials, genuine-input/security holds, owner veto/cancel, actual operational holds, PR #10’s actual PR #9 ancestry dependency and applicable exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator verifies recommendation-policy/restart/recovery, independent resolver records, exporter compatibility and activation/rollback evidence. Preserve frozen rollout sources, completed deployments, notification limits, concurrency 10, truthful lifecycle labels, authenticated responses and the single 30-minute/open-PR orchestrator with idle exit.\n- Continue coordinator monitoring and aligned repairs for PR #9 and every qualifying companion/correction PR through successful `dev` merges and required post-merge validation. This formatting correction does not complete that broader objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"a0c782b939e10dfbdb8b49208545c316cc542bd48ff9508fe22870b0a712597e","text":"# Complete PR #9’s current-base diagnostic correction\n\n## Summary\n\nPreserve the complete SQL Explorer checkpoint against pinned dev `71422731e51af15a104b65915873d576bf0024c0`.\n\nThe complete assigned feedback and failed-job logs establish import-ordering, formatting and mount-ordering failures at published head `7719e9e18fe98b18ea5ee26c3246dd1341b40f24`. They do not validate the checkpoint’s newer corrections.\n\nThe recorded answers settle the implementation choices. Finish the selected lifecycle correction and diagnostics, obtain fresh GitHub evidence, then independently plan only demonstrated rendering repairs. This plan completes the diagnostic specification; diagnostic success does not complete the parent task.\n\n## Implementation and compatibility\n\n- **Mount ordering:** Preserve and finish the saved work in `agent_tools/sql_explorer_visual_scene.py`. Register the scene’s one-shot action through the intended workspace’s existing `pending_mount_action`. Preserve prior action ownership, single invocation, replacement ownership and exception propagation.\n- Order actual workspace completion and its deferred restoration/focus application before the single database switch. Complete that switch’s restoration before requesting command focus once. Mark initialization complete only after queued command focus applies. Keep production mount/tab/restoration callbacks and ruler presentation unchanged.\n- Readiness must reject later focus loss without repairing it. Retain strict ordering, focus, equality and non-mutation assertions. Add no replacement timer, arbitrary queue drain, repeated refocus, assertion retry or trace filtering.\n- **Quality:** Verify the saved import correction and complete formatting using the repository configuration and pinned Ruff toolchain on GitHub. Preserve every import, fixture byte, parameter, assertion and negative control; introduce no suppression or baseline change.\n- **Caret comparisons:** Finish the SVG-evidence helper and capture integration. For both `keyboard-multicursor` and `editor-command-caret`, retain direct **1280×800**, actual **2560×1600 intermediate**, and once-reduced **1280×800** PNGs under both original and diagnostic-only verified DejaVu Sans Mono declarations: **twelve complete PNGs**.\n- Use identical scene/state inputs for each pair. Change only the identified terminal font declaration in diagnostic variants. Retain exact raw/framed/supersampling SVGs, actual intermediate bytes, dimensions, hashes, lengths, renderer arguments, versions and one Lanczos reduction. Ordinary production output and its invocation remain intact.\n- Retain observed font availability and bounded font-file hashes. Report renderer-selected font identity as unavailable where the API cannot expose it.\n- **Border evidence:** Finish bounded observations for `connections-searching` and `result-success`: actual border geometry, ancestor clips, resolved styles, native styled-widget/compositor edge rows, sampled coordinates and corresponding SVG/full-PNG evidence. Select no production border repair before identifying the failing layer.\n- Preserve raw-strip fidelity alongside strict native-styled-widget/compositor equality, including trailing spaces, combining marks, wide cells and colors/styles.\n- Update focused diagnostic documentation and the existing managed changelog fragment. Preserve recovered source/docs, historical releases, complete task history and current-dev capture/provenance safeguards. Fully read files before editing.\n\nPublic APIs, production signatures, dependencies and Python **3.8–3.14** compatibility remain unchanged. Diagnostic fields are additive; existing fields retain their meanings. Preserve all existing bounds, including separate **4 MiB SVG/decoded-PNG comparison budgets**, reduced-diagnostic limits and exporter **8 MiB per-file / 64 MiB total** limits. Missing, failed or oversized evidence remains incomplete.\n\n## Complete feature contract retained\n\n- Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down extends anchored selections without creating cursors; preserve independent preferred columns, reversal, short-line clamping and boundaries.\n- Preserve independent and same-row multicursors, selection merging, movement/editing and exact-position Shift+Up/Down toggles.\n- Ctrl+C, `cp` and Ctrl+X record document-order fragments, including empties. All-empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor copies the whole buffer.\n- Keyboard, command and terminal paste distribute matching fragments first, matching lines second—ignoring one trailing line ending—then repeat the whole text. Preserve metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Preserve atomic undo/redo, shared bounded history recording/pruning and document-reset cleanup.\n- Keep thin primary/secondary underlines over existing text, spaces and expanded tabs, with bars only in padding. Preserve SQL, colors, widths, selections, wrapping, scrolling, ruler/completion mapping and suffixes.\n- Retain selected narrow UI/fixture, journal, new-file, picker, menu, help, find and export repairs, supersampling and ruler reassessment. Partial implementation establishes no additional scope.\n\n## Focused regressions and GitHub acceptance\n\nAll installs, programs, tests, probes and rendering execute through GitHub; private workers perform source-only work.\n\n1. Obtain separate independent review of this complete current-base plan before coding.\n2. Run deterministic delayed-mount coverage first. Prove switching/readiness/capture remain blocked before completion; preserve action ownership and exceptions; require restorations before initialization, exactly one database action and command-focus request, and readiness after actual focus application. Retain later-focus-loss rejection and independent production tab-restoration coverage.\n3. Run caret-stage regressions for exact bytes/hashes, dimensions, declaration-only changes, actual invocation identity, one reduction, non-mutation, missing fonts, renderer failures and exact budget boundaries.\n4. Run border regressions covering coordinates, clipping, Unicode/styles, missing layers, shared bounds and non-mutation. Retain shifted/missing-cell and changed-style negative controls.\n5. Run affected lifecycle, ruler, styled-row, diagnostic and capture suites across Textual **0.73.0** and **0.89.1**, followed by focused selection/multicursor, clipboard, history/reset, caret/completion, journal, menu and checkbox/selector coverage. Keep test modules within repository size limits.\n6. Require exact-final-head lint/format/type, quality, canonical coverage JSON, artifact, supported-Python/minimum-dependency, SDK and aggregate fast checks. Preserve **98.03% branch**, **98.92% combined**, **99.22% statement**, subsystem and debt floors.\n7. Use the existing signed `agent-visual/<candidateSHA>` temporary-candidate route, dispatch to `agent-visual.yml` on main, trusted exporter and geometry-JSON transport. No new dispatcher, native-profile deployment or sidecar transport is required.\n8. Bind evidence to actual source/checkpoint, candidate, base, task, plan, dependencies, producer/consumer revisions, run/job/attempt and artifact hashes. Verify extracted bytes and actual transport sizes.\n9. Independently inspect all twelve full stage PNGs and map the caret cells across stages. Inspect border layers and retain contradictory or inconclusive findings. Underline flags alone cannot establish raster visibility.\n10. After evidence demonstrates a cause, obtain a separate concrete repair plan and independent review before implementing the narrow repair with a meaningful causal regression.\n11. Before correction publication, require complete independent feature/source/companion assessment and all **46 geometry checks plus individual full 1280×800 PNG verdicts at 208×47 cells**. Keep existing rejections effective until fresh acceptance; historical captures cannot certify new content.\n\n## Authority, dependencies and completion\n\n- The inspected prerequisite catalogues establish no upstream peer-merge requirement for PR #9. Do not fabricate `pr_dev_merge` dependencies or treat legacy review migration as satisfaction.\n- Preserve PR #10’s actual PR #9 dev-merge/ancestry requirement and PR #37’s separate dependency on #39. Separate native-profile tasks retain their own scope and approvals.\n- Trusted coordination must recheck current head/base/request, provenance, credentials, authorization and genuine holds at each action boundary. Recorded observations and recommendation selections grant no protected exact-head approval or hold release.\n- Preserve complete questions/options/answers, independent resolver records, owner veto/cancel, frozen rollout bytes and completed/cancelled operations. Do not repeat completed deployments.\n- Retain companion recommendation-policy/restart/recovery and applicable exporter/producer-consumer activation/rollback verification. Preserve authenticated responses, notification limits, concurrency **10**, truthful exclusive lifecycle labels including `agent:writing`, and one **30-minute** orchestrator while qualifying PRs remain open, with idle exit.\n- Continue coordinator monitoring and aligned repairs until PR #9 and every qualifying companion/correction/repair PR merge successfully into `dev` and required post-merge validation completes. This diagnostic checkpoint does not replace that completion requirement.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"593dc98c93f012c7fe21569be941f7275f643388f3b541521965fc014932eba7","text":"# Complete PR #9’s correction against current dev\n\n## Summary\n\nPreserve the complete SQL Explorer checkpoint and reconcile it against pinned dev `04945ba5c60f15eead12ccefdbfb4b7932284dc9`.\n\nComplete feedback for published head `c3f65825400fe53185e6dbcefd1e730d0b005aff` identifies five new lint findings, four formatting findings, and an off-center new-file dialog. The inspected PNG and settled geometry confirm that `NewSqlFileScreen` resolves to left/top alignment despite its base screen’s center/middle contract.\n\nThe recorded **Scoped alignment**, **Preserve current dev**, and **Preserve dev matrix** decisions settle this correction. No additional owner preference is needed. Obtain fresh independent review of this complete current-base plan before coding.\n\n## Implementation and compatibility\n\n- **Restore incoming dev safeguards.** Remove stale reversions of inherited capture-isolation, sandbox, probe, source-validation and coordinator-authority modules; their tests, support modules, task-evidence records and workflow safeguards. Preserve their pinned-dev contracts, fixed identities, admission checks, cleanup, security and aggregate-check behavior.\n- Restore unrelated inherited automation files exactly from pinned dev. Reconcile shared documentation and changelog content, retaining dev history, feature-specific activation documentation and every distinct feature entry. Preserve recovered source/documentation and complete authenticated task history.\n- **Reconcile validation configuration.** Use current dev’s `.github/workflows/tests.yml` and `tox.ini` as the baseline, retaining native/source-validation modes and their guards. Reapply only PR #9’s necessary `Pillow>=10,<13` test dependencies and canonical coverage JSON upload.\n- Preserve Python **3.9–3.14** runtime profiles, `py39-min`, both Python 3.10 SDK profiles, compile/tests, minimum-declaration validation and `pip check`. Remove stale Python 3.8 runtime-profile/interpreter/constraints reversions across scripts, tests and documentation. Keep current dev’s minimum pins unchanged.\n- Preserve public `>=3.8,<3.15` metadata, Python 3.8 static syntax targets, public APIs, runtime dependencies and supported Textual compatibility. Do not describe Python 3.9 runtime results as Python 3.8 validation.\n- **Center the SQL dialog.** In `analytics_toolkit/sql_explorer/file_commands.py`, explicitly include `NewSqlFileScreen` in the existing `NewFileScreen` center/middle selector. Preserve dialog dimensions, controls, filename validation, focus and save/cancel behavior.\n- **Correct all reported quality findings.** Fix E501 in the render-diagnostics helper, border-diagnostics tests and supersampling tests; I001 in styled-row tests; and PLW0108 in visual-state tests. Use a named forwarding callback where necessary to preserve invocation behavior. Apply canonical formatting to the four reported modules using Ruff **0.15.22**, the configured 100-character limit and LF endings.\n- Preserve every assertion, fixture byte, parameter, Unicode/style expectation, negative control and diagnostic output. Add no suppressions, skips or debt-baseline changes. Fully read each edited file through its final continuation before writing.\n- Retain the managed changelog fragment without changing package or README versions.\n\n## Complete feature and diagnostic contract\n\n- Preserve anchored Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down selection without spawning cursors; independent preferred columns, reversal, clamping and boundaries; independent and same-row multicursors, selection merging and exact-position Shift+Up/Down toggles.\n- Preserve document-order Ctrl+C/`cp`/Ctrl+X fragments, including empties. All-empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor copies the whole buffer.\n- Preserve shared keyboard/command/terminal paste precedence: matching fragments, matching lines while ignoring one trailing line ending, then whole-text repetition. Retain metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Preserve atomic editing/undo/redo, shared bounded history recording/pruning and document-reset cleanup.\n- Preserve thin primary/secondary underlines over existing text, spaces and expanded tabs; bars only in padding. Retain SQL, colors, widths, selections, wrapping, scroll/ruler/completion mapping and suffixes.\n- Retain selected narrow UI/fixture/journal/picker/menu/help/find/export repairs, supersampling, ruler presentation/reassessment and faithful Unicode/style diagnostics.\n- Preserve mount-hook ordering: actual workspace completion and restoration precede the single database switch; its restoration precedes one command-focus request; readiness follows real focus application. Production callbacks remain unchanged and execute exactly once. Retain delayed-mount, ownership, exception, focus-loss and non-mutation coverage.\n- Preserve strict native styled-widget/compositor comparisons alongside separately identified unpadded raw strips. Do not trim, manufacture padding, force focus, retry assertions or filter lifecycle traces.\n- Retain the supplied twelve caret-stage PNGs and associated evidence. Fresh captures must preserve both scenes, original/diagnostic-only DejaVu declarations, direct/intermediate/reduced stages, exact SVGs, actual PNG bytes, hashes, settings and font observations. Preserve border diagnostics and existing transport limits; incomplete evidence remains incomplete.\n- This correction selects no new production caret, font, ruler or border presentation. Any demonstrated remaining cause requires a separate concrete repair plan and independent review.\n\n## Focused regressions and GitHub validation\n\nAll candidate execution occurs through GitHub. Private workers execute no programs, imports, tests, installs, probes or rendering.\n\n1. Add mounted centering coverage for both the base filename screen and SQL subclass, including resize. Assert resolved center/middle alignment, dialog containment and opposing margins differing by at most one terminal cell. Preserve input focus and confirm/cancel behavior. Extend new-file scene geometry checks to detect the demonstrated upper-left placement.\n2. Verify the five lint and four formatting corrections first. Formatting alone needs no new tests.\n3. Run affected diagnostic, styled-row, supersampling and visual-state modules across Textual **0.73.0** and **0.89.1**. Retain deterministic delayed-mount ordering, raw fidelity, strict styled/compositor equality, observation non-mutation and all negative controls.\n4. Run restored capture/source-validation, coordinator-authority and Python-profile regressions. Verify inherited files and evidence records retain pinned-dev bytes where no feature integration is required.\n5. Run focused selection/multicursor, clipboard, history/reset, native caret/completion, ruler, journal, menu and checkbox/selector coverage.\n6. Require fresh exact-final-head lint/format/type/quality, artifact, compatibility/minimum-dependency, SDK and aggregate fast checks. Retain canonical coverage JSON and **98.03% branch**, **98.92% combined**, **99.22% statement**, subsystem and debt floors.\n7. Use the existing trusted temporary-candidate capture route, with current producer/consumer and authority checks performed by the coordinator. Preserving native sources on dev does not establish deployment or create a new PR #9 prerequisite.\n8. Bind evidence to actual source, checkpoint, candidate, base, task, plan, dependencies, producer/consumer, run/job/attempt and artifact hashes. Independently inspect every retained caret-stage PNG and relevant border layers; historical findings and successful capture jobs cannot certify new content.\n9. Before correction publication, require complete independent feature/source/companion assessment and all **46 geometry checks plus individual full 1280×800 PNG verdicts at 208×47 cells**. Preserve existing rejections until fresh independent acceptance.\n\n## Delivery, authority and completion\n\n- Revalidate if head or dev advances; transfer no historical plan, CI or visual approval.\n- Preserve genuine credential, authentication, security, provenance, owner-input/veto/cancel, operational and protected exact-head gates. Recommendation selections and historical control observations release none.\n- Preserve frozen rollout bytes and completed/cancelled operations. Reconciliation does not authorize deployment or rerunning completed rollouts.\n- Retain companion recommendation-policy work, independent full-task resolution, authenticated question/answer records and safe recovery of agents waiting solely on routine choices. Preserve genuine-input and security holds.\n- Preserve actual dependency direction: PR #10 requires PR #9’s successful dev merge and ancestry; PR #37 retains its separate PR #39 dependency. Do not invent upstream peer-merge prerequisites for PR #9.\n- Retain concurrency **10**, truthful exclusive lifecycle labels including `agent:writing`, notification limits, authenticated responses and one **30-minute** open-PR orchestrator with idle exit.\n- The coordinator continues monitoring and aligned repairs until PR #9 and every qualifying companion/correction/repair PR merge successfully into `dev` and required post-merge validation completes. This correction checkpoint does not itself complete that parent objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"a282747096ec3516174d9ce72b36c5795729a41ef107c5efc4e353c1737ce9cf","text":"# Complete PR #9’s caret export correction on current dev\n\n## Summary\n\nPreserve the complete SQL Explorer checkpoint against pinned dev `4a17e91b20b2683aca365f486e6217a141ef8c5b`. Finish the selected fixture, export-underline, CI-provisioning and lossless-storage corrections, then obtain fresh independent review and GitHub validation.\n\nComplete assigned feedback still records failed CI and a missing editor caret for published head `66730f9b4c6cb00524758e156a772b98317c256a`. Those results do not validate saved edits. All material implementation choices are now resolved; their selections supply no plan, source, visual or protected approval.\n\n## Implementation and compatibility\n\n- **Preserve incoming dev.** Restore inherited lifecycle diagnostic modules, their tests, read-only preparation/discovery tests and PR39/PR48 evidence records from immutable pinned dev. Remove stale deletions without changing those separate tasks’ frozen identities or activating their workflows. Reconcile shared documentation and changelog history, retaining every distinct dev and feature entry.\n- **Complete the new-file fixture.** Retain the saved fake screen’s centered viewport/dialog geometry, resolved center/middle alignment and selector-specific `query_one`. Preserve required-control/button queries, all five visibility states, exact stale-evidence bytes, atomic-refresh assertions and real mounted centering/resize regressions.\n- **Finish quality corrections.** Verify the recorded import-order and formatting fixes with the actual pinned Ruff configuration on GitHub. Remove only the extra EOF blank line in `tests/agent_tools/underline_geometry.py`. Preserve every assertion, parameter, fixture value, Unicode/style expectation and negative control; add no suppression or baseline change.\n- **Store captured SVGs losslessly.** Replace the two tracked SVG fixtures with whitespace-clean `.svg.json` envelopes containing base64 content, decoded byte length and decoded SHA256. Update their provenance paths and raster-test loader. Decode strictly and verify the existing original hashes before UTF-8 decoding or replay. Record envelope identity separately; never trim or normalize captured SVG bytes.\n- Preserve recovered source/documentation and complete authenticated task history. Fully read every affected file through its final continuation before editing. Update the existing managed changelog fragment and focused capture documentation without changing package or README versions.\n\nPublic APIs, runtime dependencies, package extras and `>=3.8,<3.15` metadata remain unchanged. Preserve Python 3.8 static compatibility, current dev’s Python 3.9–3.14 runtime profiles, `py39-min`, both Python 3.10 SDK profiles and minimum dependency pins.\n\n### Export-only underline representation\n\nFinish `normalize_terminal_underlines` in `agent_tools/sql_explorer_svg_underlines.py`, integrated by `rasterize_framed_svg` before supersampling. Keep `_frame_svg`, production terminal rendering and scene state unchanged.\n\n- Process actual underlined terminal SVG spans using resolved generated-Rich class, inline and inherited styles. Derive horizontal extent from `x` and `textLength`, independently positioned spans from their own geometry, and color from resolved decoration/foreground styling.\n- Use a butt-ended thin stroke at `baseline + 0.1 × font-size`, with thickness `0.1 × font-size`. Apply existing transforms, clips, opacity and visibility exactly once in the span’s geometric context.\n- Preserve original text nodes, SQL, whitespace, glyph positions, colors, widths and clips. Use declared span width for spaces, expanded tabs, wide glyphs and combining sequences rather than counting code points.\n- Suppress only the represented native underline decoration in the normalized copy, preserving other decorations. Require idempotence. Inputs without qualifying underlines return unchanged.\n- Reject ambiguous or unsupported positioning, styles or clipping explicitly. Do not synthesize missing carets, hardcode scene coordinates, change fonts, introduce bars/blocks or silently fall back to the rejected representation.\n- Preserve exact raw/framed originals and separately identify normalized framed/supersampling SVGs, conversion records and hashes. Keep the actual 2560×1600 intermediate and exactly one Lanczos reduction to 1280×800.\n\n### CI and evidence interfaces\n\nRetain test-only `Pillow>=10,<13` and selected `resvg-py>=0.5,<0.6` dependencies in tox latest/minimum/coverage and both ordinary GitHub installation commands. Provision fontconfig/DejaVu on GitHub and explicitly run the real raster regression before the full suite. Preserve canonical coverage JSON upload and ordinary aggregate gates.\n\nKeep diagnostic additions compatible and additive. Preserve the twelve original caret-stage PNGs across both scenes, font declarations and three stages. Retain separately labeled normalized comparisons alongside them; only actual normalized ordinary invocation bytes may be identified as reused ordinary output.\n\nMaintain separate 4 MiB SVG and decoded-PNG comparison budgets, existing diagnostic bounds, and exporter limits of 8 MiB per file/64 MiB total. Missing, failed or oversized evidence remains incomplete.\n\n## Complete feature contract retained\n\n- Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down extends anchored selections across logical lines without spawning cursors. Preserve independent preferred columns, reversal, clamping and boundaries.\n- Preserve independent and same-row multicursors, merging, movement/editing and exact-position Shift+Up/Down toggles.\n- Ctrl+C, `cp` and Ctrl+X record document-order fragments including empties. All-empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Keyboard, command and terminal paste use matching fragments, then matching lines ignoring one trailing line ending, then whole-text repetition. Preserve clipboard transports, metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Preserve atomic undo/redo, shared bounded history/pruning and reset cleanup.\n- Keep thin primary/secondary underlines over occupied text, spaces and expanded tabs, including command focus